      ":question/id": "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4406",
      ":question/problem": "Find $CD$, if \n![](images/1a/1a753977affc5cc3dda18c9206116e1132254bccebd1e3f2545bea75bcc38f18.png)\nand \n![](images/b9/b99016bca94adc5de11eddef950fa13fc4349aaf95387468d07f294c409d029d.png)",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/64/64b831a66cdd9a3176d1eb916dfae189b41eb1f0f3ed3184797f92e404957878.png)"
    },
